Subject: [PATCH 06894/11362] [outer-loop] ARC su15 round-6: honest null,
 closest L9 attempt yet

Round-6 codex gpt-5.6-sol attempt on su15 landed the strongest L9 line so
far: merged the two 6 pieces into f, socketed f, converted 8 into c, and
collapsed three of four hunters in one transition while preserving both
required fruits intact. The final 7 couldn't merge before the resource
meter expired. New findings: sockets can strand remaining hunters if
socketed too early; hunter composites can be fully occluded behind a
fruit (undercounting risk from rendered frames); socket overlap is NOT
protection (pushing f deeper degraded c to b); the resource meter charges
multiple cells for failed/long-distance clicks, and ACTION7's undo does
not refund it.

Honest null -- no registry count change, frontier stays at level 8, but
this is the deepest verified L9 progress recorded so far.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
